# Development-only dependencies. NOT installed by the API or worker deployment — that installs
# from requirements.lock, which is compiled from requirements.in alone.
#
# Keeping these separate is deliberate: pyarrow is imported only by
# pipelines/storage/localfs.py, which serves the OFFLINE training track. The Supabase and
# Airflow runtime uses pipelines/storage/pg.py and never touches parquet, so shipping pyarrow
# into that image would be paying for a capability that path cannot use.

# Local train track — parquet shards under data/processed/.
# Imported lazily inside localfs.py so a pg-only environment never needs it.
pyarrow>=15,<25

# Lint. The repo has a ruff.toml; without ruff installed it was decoration.
ruff>=0.16,<1

# Test runner. Nothing depends on it yet: verification today is the `main()`/`--selftest`
# idiom on each module, which needs no runner. The self-checks are written so that converting
# them into test_*.py is mechanical when that becomes worthwhile.
pytest>=8,<9
